	'ch2_intro' => 'About sixty cheeses sit on the counter at Noka Cheese, kept in six styles and cut when you ask. Each price is per 100 g.',
	'ch2_e1_e' => 'Style 01',
	'ch2_e1_h' => 'Fresh & lactic',
	'ch2_e1_now' => 'Young cow lactic, This week\'s goat lactic, and Basket-mould cow',
	'ch2_e1_p1' => 'Fresh and lactic cheeses are made from cow or goat milk and have no rind. The paste is bright, and the batches on the counter were made this week. Texture is soft and spoonable, with a clean lactic taste and none of the stickiness of a washed rind. We keep the cut face in two-layer cheese paper.',
	'ch2_e1_p2' => 'At home, leave that paper on, hold the wedge at 4–8 °C, and take it out 45 minutes before you eat. A 150 g wedge is a good amount for two. Tell us what it is for and we cut a sliver of two or three on the knife tip before we weigh your piece.',
	'ch2_e2_e' => 'Style 02',
	'ch2_e2_h' => 'Bloomy',
	'ch2_e2_now' => 'Four-week white round, Soft-edge bloomy, and Six-week cow round',
	'ch2_e2_p1' => 'Bloomy cheeses are made from cow\'s milk and wear a white rind. They are ripened for 4–6 weeks and stay soft to the edge. Near the rind the paste yields; toward the centre a younger wheel is a little firmer. We open a wheel when you ask, cut soft rinds with the wire, and weigh the wedge in front of you.',
	'ch2_e2_p2' => 'The name and the date go on the fold of the paper. Keep the wedge in that two-layer paper at 4–8 °C and take it out 45 minutes before serving so the paste can relax. If the round you wanted is finished, we say so and offer a sliver of what is actually open.',
	'ch2_e3_e' => 'Style 03',
