	'ch2_e3_now' => 'Orange brine wheel, Cellar-washed round, and Twice-washed cow wheel',
	'ch2_e3_p1' => 'Washed-rind cheeses are made from cow\'s milk and have an orange rind. In our cellar they are washed in brine twice a week. The rind is sticky and aromatic; the paste underneath is supple. Elif Arslan turns, brushes and washes the wheels at 11 °C and 92 % humidity. We cut these with the wire, weigh them in front of you, and write the name and date on the paper.',
	'ch2_e3_p2' => 'Keep the wedge wrapped, at 4–8 °C, and take it out 45 minutes before you eat. The cheese of the month is one 250 g wedge of the month\'s washed rind at €12. The style itself is from €4.90 / 100 g.',
	'ch2_e4_e' => 'Style 04',
	'ch2_e4_h' => 'Alpine',
	'ch2_e4_now' => 'Twelve-month mountain wheel, Eighteen-month alpine wheel, and Nutty hard wheel',
	'ch2_e4_p1' => 'Alpine cheeses are raw cow\'s milk, pressed hard, from 12–18-month mountain wheels. The taste is nutty. Tomás Reyes looks after this part of the counter and cuts hard wheels with the two-handled knife. We weigh every piece in front of you. 150 g is a good wedge for two. The paste is firm, some wheels show small eyes, and the rind is natural.',
	'ch2_e4_p2' => 'Vell Alpine Cooperative sends the summer-pasture wheels that stand for 18 months. Keep the wedge in two-layer cheese paper at 4–8 °C and take it out 45 minutes before serving. These are the wheels people ask for when the board needs something firm beside a soft rind.',
	'ch2_e5_e' => 'Style 05',
	'ch2_e5_h' => 'Blue',
	'ch2_e5_now' => 'October sheep blue, Cow blue from the wheel, and Winter sheep blue',
	'ch2_e5_p1' => 'Blue cheeses are made from sheep or cow milk. We cut them from the wheel and never sell them pre-packed. The piece you take home is cut while you wait, veins and all, and weighed in front of you. Lowmere Sheep Dairy makes one blue, from October to May. Outside that season we only sell the blue that is actually on the counter, or we tell you it is out.',
	'ch2_e5_p2' => 'Keep the wedge in two-layer paper at 4–8 °C and take it out 45 minutes before eating. A 150 g wedge is a good size for two. Taste a sliver on the knife tip before you decide how strong a piece you want.',
	'ch2_e6_e' => 'Style 06',
	'ch2_e6_h' => 'Goat & sheep',
	'ch2_e6_now' => 'Ash goat log, Natural-rind goat, and Seasonal sheep round',
	'ch2_e6_p1' => 'Goat and sheep cheeses come from small farms and change with the season. Rinds are natural or coated in ash. Hollin Ridge Farm sends goat cheese as fresh curd and as ash logs, with kidding in spring. An ash log shows white paste under a grey coat; a natural rind is thinner and drier. We cut soft pieces with the wire and weigh them in front of you.',
	'ch2_e6_p2' => 'The wrap is two-layer cheese paper with the name and the date on the fold, plus a line on how to keep it: paper on, 4–8 °C, out for 45 minutes before serving. When the season shifts the milk, the three names on this card shift with it.',
	'bd_eyebrow_list' => 'Boards',
	'bd_eyebrow' => 'Reserve in the shop · pickup from 11:00',
	'bd_h1' => 'Boards',
	'bd_intro' => 'Boards are the way to reserve cheese from Noka Cheese. Choose in the shop, pay online, and pick up at the counter from 11:00.',
	'bd_s1_e' => 'Three boards',
	'bd_s1_h' => 'Three boards',
	'bd_s1_p1' => 'The counter board for two has 3 cheeses, 300 g, bread and quince paste, at €26. The table board for four has 5 cheeses, 600 g, bread, quince and pickles, at €48. The long board for eight has 7 cheeses, 1.2 kg, two breads, quince and honey, at €92. Grace Owusu builds the boards. Cheeses are chosen from the six styles on the counter that day, about sixty cheeses in all, cut for the booking rather than set in plastic beforehand.',
	'bd_s1_p2' => 'Bread, quince paste, pickles and honey appear only on the boards that list them. If you would rather point at every wedge yourself, ask for the monger\'s three wedges instead of a set board.',
	'bd_s2_e' => 'Counter and tasting',
	'bd_s2_h' => 'Wedges, the month, and a tasting seat',
	'bd_s2_p1' => 'Monger\'s three wedges are 3 × 150 g chosen at the counter and wrapped, at €22. You taste, we cut with the wire or the two-handled knife, and you take the paper home. Cheese of the month is one 250 g wedge of the month\'s washed rind, at €12. Those rinds are cow\'s milk, orange, washed in brine twice a week in the cellar.',
	'bd_s2_p2' => 'Saturday tasting is a separate booking: 45 minutes, 6 cheeses, max 8 people, €18 per person, at 10:30 and 15:00, led by Grace Owusu. Samuel Adeyemi confirms every reservation by email, whether it is a board, a wedge or a seat at the tasting.',
	'bd_s3_e' => 'Reserving',
	'bd_s3_h' => 'How reserving works',
	'bd_s3_p1' => 'Choose a board in the shop and pay online. Reserve by 18:00 the day before. Pickup starts at 11:00 on the day. The counter is open Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00, Sat 09:00–17:00 and Sun 10:00–14:00. Monday is closed, so there is no Monday pickup. Samuel Adeyemi confirms every reservation by email; wait for that note before you treat the board as held.',
	'bd_s3_p2' => 'There is no delivery and no shipping. Boards are pickup only from Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Cancel by 18:00 the day before if your plans change. After that hour the board is cut for the name on the reservation.',
	'bd_s4_e' => 'Price list',
	'bd_s4_h' => 'Price list',
	'bd_s4_p1' => 'Prices are in euro and stay in euro in every language. The same six lines are on the counter, on this page, and on the shop products. Cheese cut loose, outside these boards, is priced per 100 g by style.',
	'bd_s5_e' => 'Larger tables',
	'bd_s5_h' => 'For more than eight people',
	'bd_s5_p1' => 'The long board stops at eight people. For a larger table, write to the counter with the date, the number of people and what the cheese is for. Use the form on this page, or email counter@nokacheese.example about a board for a larger table. During opening hours you can phone +00 21 4418 2290. We still cut to order, still wrap in two-layer paper, and still ask you to pick up from 11:00.',
	'bd_s5_p2' => 'We do not ship. Tell us if you want the range of all six styles or a table weighted toward washed rinds. Noa Kessler buys every wheel herself and will say if a style is out rather than fill the board with the wrong cheese.',
	'hw_eyebrow' => 'Taste · cut · wrap',
	'hw_h1' => 'How we cut',
	'hw_intro' => 'Every wedge at Noka Cheese is named, cut and wrapped for the person at the counter. The order is taste, then cut, then wrap.',
	'hw_s1_n' => '01',
	'hw_s1_h' => 'Taste',
	'hw_s1_p1' => 'Tell us what the cheese is for. A weeknight supper and a board for four are different requests, and the sliver we offer follows from that. We cut a sliver of two or three cheeses on the knife tip, from the wheels open that day. You do not have to buy the one you taste. About sixty cheeses are on the counter, in six styles: fresh and lactic, bloomy, washed rind, alpine, blue, and goat and sheep.',
	'hw_s1_p2' => 'Noa Kessler buys every wheel she would be happy to cut for a friend. If we are out of the one you hoped for, we say so, rather than steer you to a wedge she would not choose.',
	'hw_s2_n' => '02',
	'hw_s2_h' => 'Cut',
	'hw_s2_p1' => 'Washed rinds and other soft rinds are cut with the wire. Hard wheels are cut with the two-handled knife. We weigh the piece in front of you. 150 g is a good wedge for two. Fresh lactic cheese has no rind and takes the wire; bloomy rind, soft to the edge after 4–6 weeks, takes the wire as well.',
	'hw_s2_p2' => 'Alpine wheels, raw cow\'s milk and 12–18 months, take the two-handled knife. Tomás Reyes handles those hard wheels. Blue is cut from the wheel, never handed over pre-packed. Prices per 100 g are €3.20 for fresh and lactic, €4.40 for bloomy, €4.90 for washed rind, €4.60 for alpine, €4.80 for blue, and €5.40 for goat and sheep.',
	'hw_s3_n' => '03',
	'hw_s3_h' => 'Wrap',
	'hw_s3_p1' => 'We wrap in two-layer cheese paper. The name and the date are written on the fold, with a line on how to keep the wedge. At home, leave it in that paper. Keep it at 4–8 °C. Take it out 45 minutes before you eat so the paste is not cold from the fridge. At 19:00 every cut face still on the counter is re-wrapped before we clear for the night.',
	'hw_s3_p2' => 'Mei Chou wraps on weekends. If a line on the paper is hard to read, ask at the counter or write to counter@nokacheese.example. The paper is the record of what you bought: which cheese, which day, and how to hold it until you eat it.',
	'ta_eyebrow' => 'Saturdays · 10:30 and 15:00',
	'ta_h1' => 'Tastings',
	'ta_intro' => 'Saturday tastings at Noka Cheese are led by Grace Owusu. There are two sittings, six cheeses, and a seat you reserve in the shop.',
	'ta_s1_e' => 'Sittings',
	'ta_s1_h' => 'Saturday sittings',
	'ta_s1_p1' => 'Tastings run on Saturday at 10:30 and at 15:00. Each sitting is 45 minutes. You taste 6 cheeses. The group is capped at 8 people. The price is €18 per person. Grace Owusu leads both sittings; she also builds the boards. The cheeses are cut from the counter that week, across the six styles we keep, not from a flight packed in advance.',
	'ta_s1_p2' => 'Saturday hours are 09:00–17:00, so both sittings fall inside the open day. Reserve by 18:00 the day before. Board pickup is a separate queue from 11:00. A tasting seat is not a board, and a board is not a place at the table.',
	'ta_s2_e' => 'Booking',
	'ta_s2_h' => 'How to book',
	'ta_s2_p1' => 'Book the Saturday tasting as a product in the shop and pay online. Samuel Adeyemi confirms every reservation by email. If you cannot come, cancel by 18:00 the day before. There is no delivery. The tasting is at the counter, Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Phone +00 21 4418 2290 during opening hours if you are unsure which sitting still has room.',
	'ta_s2_p2' => 'The shop product is the booking path for a standard seat. Questions can also go to counter@nokacheese.example. Monday is closed, and there is no tasting on the other weekdays; the two Saturday times are the only sittings.',
	'ta_s3_e' => 'The table',
	'ta_s3_h' => 'What is on the table',
	'ta_s3_p1' => 'Six cheeses are set out for the sitting, drawn from the styles actually open: fresh and lactic, bloomy, washed rind, alpine, blue, and goat and sheep, as the week allows. Washed rinds have been brushed in the cellar at 11 °C and 92 % humidity. Alpine pieces come from 12–18-month wheels. Blue is cut from the wheel that week, never from a pre-packed piece.',
	'ta_s3_p2' => 'You get a small taste of each, water, and Grace to say what you are eating. The €18 covers the sitting, not a board to take home. If you want cheese to carry out, reserve a board or ask afterwards for a wedge. Monger\'s three wedges are €22 for 3 × 150 g, chosen at the counter and wrapped.',
	'ce_eyebrow' => '11 °C · 92 % humidity',
	'ce_h1' => 'Cellar',
	'ce_intro' => 'The ageing cellar is under the counter at Noka Cheese. It is held at 11 °C and 92 % humidity, and Elif Arslan keeps the wheels.',
	'ce_s1_e' => 'Under the shop',
	'ce_s1_h' => 'Under the shop',
	'ce_s1_p1' => 'The cellar is the small room under the shop in Old Dairy Yard, Brookmere. Temperature is 11 °C. Humidity is 92 %. Washed-rind wheels finish here, and the rest of the counter\'s cheese is held here so cut faces are not left to dry in the shop air. The shop opened in 2014.',
	'ce_s1_p2' => 'Noa Kessler still buys every wheel herself. About sixty cheeses in six styles pass through this room before they are cut upstairs. Elif starts at 07:30, before the door opens at 10:00. The cellar is her workplace through the morning; the counter above is where you taste and take a wedge home.',
	'ce_s2_e' => 'The routine',
	'ce_s2_h' => 'Elif\'s routine',
	'ce_s2_p1' => 'Elif Arslan is the cellar keeper. She turns, brushes and washes the wheels. At 07:30 she turns and brushes the cellar wheels. Washed rinds are washed in brine twice a week. The rind is orange and sticky. The work is a brush and a brine wash, done on that rhythm, not a flavour added at the counter when you order.',
	'ce_s2_p2' => 'At 09:30 the counter upstairs is set and the wires are checked. Doors open at 10:00. By 19:00 every cut face on the counter is re-wrapped and the counter is cleared. The same 11 °C and 92 % humidity cover the wheels we are finishing, including the small washed-rind wheels from Ostra Creamery.',
	'ce_s3_e' => 'Finishing',
	'ce_s3_h' => 'Wheels we finish ourselves',
	'ce_s3_p1' => 'Ostra Creamery is two cheesemakers. Their small washed-rind wheels are finished in our cellar, then cut upstairs with the wire. We also hold alpine wheels from Vell Alpine Cooperative, summer-pasture cheeses at 18 months, until Tomás Reyes cuts them with the two-handled knife. Henrik Dahl visits the four makers twice a year, and the wheels from those visits land here first.',
	'ce_s3_p2' => 'Fresh and lactic cheeses are made this week and do not take a long finish; they still rest in the cool until the counter is set. Blue from Lowmere Sheep Dairy, made October–May, is cut from the wheel upstairs and is never pre-packed. The cheese of the month is a 250 g wedge of the month\'s washed rind, at €12.',
	'mk_eyebrow' => 'Four makers · two visits a year each',
	'mk_h1' => 'Makers',
	'mk_intro' => 'Four makers supply Noka Cheese. Henrik Dahl visits each of them twice a year, and Noa Kessler buys every wheel herself.',
	'mk_s1_e' => 'Maker 01',
	'mk_s1_h' => 'Hollin Ridge Farm',
	'mk_s1_p1' => 'Hollin Ridge Farm is a goat farm. The cheeses we take are fresh and ash logs, and kidding is in spring, so the milk is seasonal. On our counter they sit with the goat and sheep style: natural or ash rind, from €5.40 / 100 g. The fresh cheese is bright and made to eat this week. The ash log shows a white paste under a grey coat. We cut a sliver on the knife tip if you are choosing, then cut the wedge with the wire and weigh it in front of you.',
	'mk_s1_p2' => 'Henrik Dahl visits Hollin Ridge twice a year, on the same round as the other three makers. Noa buys only wheels she would cut for a friend. When the spring milk changes the cheese, the note on the counter changes with it. If the log you want is finished, we say we are out.',
	'mk_s2_e' => 'Maker 02',
	'mk_s2_h' => 'Ostra Creamery',
	'mk_s2_p1' => 'Ostra Creamery is two cheesemakers. They make small washed-rind wheels, and those wheels are finished in our cellar under the shop. Elif Arslan turns, brushes and washes them at 11 °C and 92 % humidity, in brine twice a week. The rind becomes orange and sticky. Upstairs the style is washed rind, cow\'s milk, from €4.90 / 100 g. The cheese of the month is one 250 g wedge from this style, at €12.',
	'mk_s2_p2' => 'Henrik visits Ostra twice a year. The finish still happens in Brookmere. We cut these wheels with the wire, weigh them in front of you, and write the name and date on two-layer cheese paper. A 150 g wedge is a good size for two. The creamery does not send us a pre-cut packet.',
	'mk_s3_e' => 'Maker 03',
	'mk_s3_h' => 'Vell Alpine Cooperative',
	'mk_s3_p1' => 'Vell Alpine Cooperative makes summer-pasture wheels that we keep for 18 months. The style on the counter is alpine: raw cow\'s milk, hard, 12–18-month mountain wheels, nutty, from €4.60 / 100 g. Tomás Reyes cuts this part of the counter with the two-handled knife. The paste is firm. Some wheels show small eyes. We weigh every piece in front of you and wrap it with the name and the date.',
	'mk_s3_p2' => 'Henrik Dahl visits the cooperative twice a year. Wheels come from summer pasture and stand to 18 months before we cut them. They suit a long board or a plain wedge with bread. What is open on the day you collect decides which mountain wheel goes onto a board, not a fixed slot we promise in advance.',
	'mk_s4_e' => 'Maker 04',
	'mk_s4_h' => 'Lowmere Sheep Dairy',
	'mk_s4_p1' => 'Lowmere Sheep Dairy makes one blue, from October to May. Outside those months we do not stand in for them with a cheese they did not make. We sell the cow or sheep blue that is actually on the counter, or we tell you the sheep blue is out. Blue is cut from the wheel and never pre-packed. The style is from €4.80 / 100 g.',
	'mk_s4_p2' => 'Henrik visits Lowmere twice a year. The blue is for a sliver on the knife tip and for a wedge wrapped in two-layer paper. When Grace Owusu sets six cheeses on a Saturday, blue is among them if the wheel is open. October–May is the only production window this dairy gives us.',
	'ab_eyebrow' => 'One counter · since 2014',
	'ab_h1' => 'About',
	'ab_intro' => 'Noka Cheese is an independent cheese shop with one counter and a small ageing cellar under it, in Brookmere since 2014.',
	'ab_s1_e' => 'Since 2014',
	'ab_s1_h' => 'Since 2014',
	'ab_s1_p1' => 'Noa Kessler founded the shop in 2014 and is still head monger. She buys every wheel herself and looks after the washed rinds. The counter holds about sixty cheeses in six styles. There is one counter, and the cellar is beneath it. We do not run a second shop. Hours are Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00, Sat 09:00–17:00, Sun 10:00–14:00, and Monday closed.',
	'ab_s1_p2' => 'The address is Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Phone +00 21 4418 2290. Email counter@nokacheese.example. Boards are reserved in the shop, paid online, and picked up from 11:00. Reservations close at 18:00 the day before. Samuel Adeyemi confirms each one by email.',
	'ab_p1_n' => 'Noa Kessler,',
	'ab_p1_r' => 'Founder and head monger since 2014, keeps the washed rinds and buys every wheel herself.',
	'ab_p2_n' => 'Elif Arslan,',
	'ab_p2_r' => 'Cellar keeper, turns, brushes and washes the wheels at 11 °C and 92 % humidity.',
	'ab_p3_n' => 'Tomás Reyes,',
	'ab_p3_r' => 'Counter monger, takes alpine and long-aged hard cheeses.',
	'ab_p4_n' => 'Grace Owusu',
	'ab_p4_r' => 'Looks after boards and the Saturday tastings.',
	'ab_p5_n' => 'Henrik Dahl',
	'ab_p5_r' => 'Sources; he visits the four makers twice a year.',
	'ab_p6_n' => 'Mei Chou',
	'ab_p6_r' => 'Is on the counter and the wrapping at weekends.',
	'ab_p7_n' => 'Samuel Adeyemi',
	'ab_p7_r' => 'Takes orders and pickups and confirms every reservation by email.',
	'ab_s2_e' => 'Seven people',
	'ab_s2_h' => 'Seven people',
	'ab_s2_p1' => 'On Saturday Grace leads the 10:30 and 15:00 tastings while Mei wraps. At 14:00 Samuel confirms the reservations for the next day.',
	'ab_d1_t' => '07:30',
	'ab_d1_x' => 'Elif turns and brushes the cellar wheels.',
	'ab_d2_t' => '09:30',
	'ab_d2_x' => 'The counter is set and the wires are checked.',
	'ab_d3_t' => '10:00',
	'ab_d3_x' => 'Doors open.',
	'ab_d4_t' => '11:00',
	'ab_d4_x' => 'Board pickups start.',
	'ab_d5_t' => '14:00',
	'ab_d5_x' => 'Samuel confirms tomorrow\'s reservations.',
	'ab_d6_t' => '18:00',
	'ab_d6_x' => 'Reservations close for the next day.',
	'ab_d7_t' => '19:00',
	'ab_d7_x' => 'Every cut face is re-wrapped and the counter cleared.',
	'ab_s3_e' => 'A day',
	'ab_s3_h' => 'A day at the counter',
	'ab_s3_p1' => 'Sunday closes earlier, at 14:00, and Saturday opens at 09:00. Monday the counter stays shut. The day does not change how a wedge is chosen. You say what it is for, you taste two or three slivers on the knife tip, we cut with the wire or the two-handled knife, we weigh the piece, and we wrap it with the name and the date.',
	'vi_eyebrow' => 'Brookmere · Tue–Sun',
	'vi_h1' => 'Visit',
	'vi_intro' => 'The counter is at Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Come for a wedge, or pick up a board you have reserved.',
	'vi_lbl_address' => 'Address',
	'vi_lbl_hours' => 'Hours',
	'vi_lbl_phone' => 'Phone',
	'vi_lbl_email' => 'Email',
	'vi_addr' => 'Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere',
	'vi_hours' => 'Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00 · Sat 09:00–17:00 · Sun 10:00–14:00 · Mon closed',
	'vi_s1_e' => 'Find us',
	'vi_s1_h' => 'Address and hours',
	'vi_s1_p1' => 'Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Phone +00 21 4418 2290. Email counter@nokacheese.example. Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00. Sat 09:00–17:00. Sun 10:00–14:00. Monday closed. Board pickup runs from 11:00. Reserve by 18:00 the day before. Saturday tastings are at 10:30 and 15:00. Elif Arslan is with the cellar wheels at 07:30, and the door you use opens at 10:00.',
	'vi_s1_p2' => 'Write to the counter for a board larger than eight, or use the form on this page. A call during opening hours reaches the counter. Samuel Adeyemi confirms reservations by email, so read that note before you come for a pickup.',
	'vi_s2_e' => 'Directions',
	'vi_s2_h' => 'Directions',
	'vi_s2_p1' => 'The shop is in Old Dairy Yard at 9 Tannery Lane, in Brookmere. Come along Tannery Lane and into Old Dairy Yard; the counter is at number 9. From the tram stop, walk to Tannery Lane and then into the yard. Those are the two ways in: the lane, then the yard. There is no second address and no delivery door.',
	'vi_s2_p2' => 'Look for the one counter. If the yard is unfamiliar, call +00 21 4418 2290 while we are open and we will get you from the lane to the door. Boards are handed over at that counter from 11:00. We do not pass a bag at the tram stop, and we do not leave an order outside the hours above.',
	'vi_s3_e' => 'Pickup',
	'vi_s3_h' => 'Pickup',
	'vi_s3_p1' => 'Pickup is at the counter only. We do not ship. Reserve a board in the shop and pay online by 18:00 the day before. Pickup starts at 11:00. Samuel Adeyemi confirms by email. If you are collecting monger\'s three wedges, those are chosen at the counter, 3 × 150 g, wrapped, at €22, so allow time to taste two or three slivers first.',
	'vi_s3_p2' => 'Cheese of the month can be reserved ahead: one 250 g washed-rind wedge at €12. Sunday pickup ends at 14:00. Saturday pickup ends at 17:00. From Tuesday to Friday the counter is open until 19:00. Cancel a board by 18:00 the day before.',
	'vi_s4_e' => 'Write to us',
	'vi_s4_h' => 'Write to the counter',
	'vi_s4_p1' => 'Use the form on this page for a note to the counter. It asks for your name, your email, a phone number if you want to leave one, the date you want, the number of people, and a message. A consent checkbox sits with those fields. The button reads Send to the counter. If the form tool is not available, the page offers an email button to counter@nokacheese.example instead.',
	'vi_s4_p2' => 'For a larger board, say how many people and what the cheese is for. A standard Saturday tasting is still booked in the shop at €18 a person. We answer from the counter email. We do not ship cheese.',
	'ar_call' => 'Call +00 21 4418 2290 →',
	'nl_eyebrow' => 'Monthly · from the counter',
	'nl_h1' => 'Counter letter',
	'nl_intro' => 'The Counter letter is one letter a month from Noka Cheese, about the cellar, the cheese of the month, and the tasting dates.',
	'nl_s1_e' => 'Inside',
	'nl_s1_h' => 'What the letter carries',
	'nl_s1_p1' => 'Once a month we write what is in the cellar, name the cheese of the month, and list the Saturday tasting dates. The cheese of the month is one 250 g wedge of that month\'s washed rind, at €12. Tastings stay at 10:30 and 15:00, 45 minutes, six cheeses, eight people at most, €18 a person, with Grace Owusu.',
	'nl_s1_p2' => 'The letter does not replace the counter. Hours in it match the door: Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00, Sat 09:00–17:00, Sun 10:00–14:00, Monday closed. Pickup is from 11:00. Reservations close at 18:00 the day before. You can unsubscribe any time, and one letter a month is the whole rhythm.',
	'nl_s2_e' => 'Cellar notes',
	'nl_s2_h' => 'Notes from the cellar',
	'nl_s2_p1' => 'The letter says what Elif Arslan is turning at 11 °C and 92 % humidity, and which washed rinds were brushed in brine. It may mention Ostra Creamery wheels finishing under the shop, or the alpine wheels standing to 18 months. It is not a list of all sixty cheeses. You still choose at the counter by tasting two or three slivers.',
	'nl_s2_p2' => 'A note in the letter is an invitation to come, not a parcel we post. We do not ship cheese. If a wheel we mentioned is finished by the time you visit, we tell you we are out. Noa would rather do that than sell the wrong one.',
	'nl_s3_e' => 'Join',
	'nl_s3_h' => 'How to join',
	'nl_s3_p1' => 'Add your email in the form on this page and send it to subscribe to the Counter letter. If no form tool is running, the form opens your email app addressed to counter@nokacheese.example. The notice on that path says you are not subscribed until you send the message. We send one letter a month.',
	'nl_s3_p2' => 'You can unsubscribe any time. The address is for this letter. Reservation mail is separate: Samuel Adeyemi writes those confirmations because you booked a board or a tasting. The footer of the site links here. Read the privacy page for how a message you send to the counter is kept.',
	'pv_eyebrow' => 'Legal',
	'pv_h1' => 'Privacy',
	'pv_intro' => 'This page says what Noka Cheese does with the details you send to the counter at Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere.',
	'pv_s1_e' => 'Section 01',
	'pv_s1_h' => 'What we collect',
	'pv_s1_p1' => 'When you reserve a board or a tasting, we take the name, email and order details needed to confirm pickup. Samuel Adeyemi confirms every reservation by email. The contact form also asks for phone, which you may skip, the date you want, the number of people, a message, and a consent checkbox. The newsletter form collects an email for the Counter letter, one letter a month.',
	'pv_s1_p2' => 'If you use the email button instead, your message goes to counter@nokacheese.example from your own mail app. We do not ask you to type a payment card number into the contact form. Payment for a reserved board happens in the shop checkout. The counter phone is +00 21 4418 2290.',
	'pv_s2_e' => 'Section 02',
	'pv_s2_h' => 'Why we use it',
	'pv_s2_p1' => 'We use reservation details to cut the board, hold it for pickup from 11:00, and send the confirmation. We use a contact message to answer the question you sent, including a board for more than eight people. We use a newsletter address to send the monthly letter until you unsubscribe. We do not sell these details.',
	'pv_s2_p2' => 'We do not add you to the Counter letter because you bought a wedge; the letter goes to people who asked for it. You can unsubscribe any time. To correct a reservation, write to counter@nokacheese.example or call during opening hours: Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00, Sat 09:00–17:00, Sun 10:00–14:00. Monday the counter is closed.',
	'pv_s3_e' => 'Section 03',
	'pv_s3_h' => 'Who sees a message',
	'pv_s3_p1' => 'Reservation notes are kept long enough to finish pickup and to handle a cancellation made by 18:00 the day before. A newsletter address stays until you unsubscribe. Samuel Adeyemi sees orders and pickups because that is his work. A question sent to the counter is read by the people answering the counter that day. We do not ship, so we do not pass a street address to a carrier for delivery.',
	'pv_s3_p2' => 'The shop can hold a basket while you check out a reservation. Seven people work at Noka Cheese; a cellar note for Elif is not the same as a booking for Samuel. Questions about this page go to counter@nokacheese.example.',
	'tm_eyebrow' => 'Legal',
	'tm_h1' => 'Terms',
	'tm_intro' => 'These terms cover sales at Noka Cheese. Cheese is sold at the counter and reserved for pickup. We do not ship.',
	'tm_s1_e' => 'Section 01',
	'tm_s1_h' => 'Sale and pickup',
	'tm_s1_p1' => 'You may buy a wedge at the counter during opening hours, or reserve a listed item in the shop: a board, the monger\'s three wedges, the cheese of the month, or a Saturday tasting. You pay online for a reservation. You pick up at Old Dairy Yard, 9 Tannery Lane, Brookmere. Pickup starts at 11:00. There is no shipping and no delivery.',
	'tm_s1_p2' => 'Hours are Tue–Fri 10:00–19:00, Sat 09:00–17:00, Sun 10:00–14:00, Monday closed. Prices are €26 for the counter board for two, €48 for the table board for four, €92 for the long board for eight, €22 for monger\'s three wedges, €12 for the cheese of the month, and €18 per person for the Saturday tasting. Loose cheese is priced per 100 g by style.',
	'tm_s2_e' => 'Section 02',
	'tm_s2_h' => 'Reservations and cancellation',
	'tm_s2_p1' => 'Reserve by 18:00 the day before. At 18:00, reservations close for the next day. Samuel Adeyemi confirms every reservation by email. Wait for that message before you treat the board as held. You may cancel until 18:00 the day before. A tasting seat uses the same clock: Saturday at 10:30 or 15:00, 45 minutes, 6 cheeses, maximum 8 people.',
	'tm_s2_p2' => 'If you do not collect, contact the counter on +00 21 4418 2290 or at counter@nokacheese.example while we are open. We hand boards over at the counter only. We do not leave a board at the tram stop, on Tannery Lane, or with anyone who is not collecting in the shop.',
	'tm_s3_e' => 'Section 03',
	'tm_s3_h' => 'Allergens',
	'tm_s3_p1' => 'Cheeses are made from cow, goat or sheep milk, as the style on the card states. Washed rinds are washed in brine. Boards include other foods only where the item says so. The counter board for two includes bread and quince paste. The table board for four includes bread, quince and pickles. The long board for eight includes two breads, quince and honey. Monger\'s three wedges and the cheese of the month are cheese, wrapped, without those extras.',
	'tm_s3_p2' => 'Tell us at the counter if you need to avoid a milk or bread. We cut with a wire or a two-handled knife that also cuts other cheeses, so we cannot promise a surface that has touched only one milk. We will tell you which milk a wheel is. A Saturday tasting is 6 cheeses; ask Grace Owusu before you book if that mix is a concern.',
	// END inner
);
